{"step_index":1449,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-11T23:52:24Z","thinking":"**Examining available mathematical tools**\n\nThe goal is to prove `prove_e20263a9`. Considering the available lemmas, `Candidate` looks relevant, connecting graph properties with roman domination number. Exploring how this lemma can be applied to the current problem is the next step. I'm focusing on identifying the properties needed for `Candidate` to be invoked, specifically, those that are provided or can be deduced in the context of `prove_e20263a9`.\n\n\n**Analyzing remaining cases for proof**\n\nThe goal is to show `radius G + 1 <= romanWeight f` for any Roman dominating function `f`. Several cases are handled; the remaining case is when at least two distinct vertices have value 2 under `f`. In this scenario, `romanWeight f` must be at least 4.\n\nIf `romanWeight f` is at least 4, then a sub-case arises where it is needed to prove `radius G <= 3`. The objective now is to use these observations to find the relationship between the graph radius and `romanWeight`.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"run_command","args":{"CommandLine":"ls -la reference/","Cwd":"/mnt/home/japake298/project/GraphConjecturing/handoff/promising13/task_e20263a9","WaitMsBeforeAsync":5000,"toolAction":"List reference directory","toolSummary":"List reference files"}}]}
